0,Music of Tonga - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Music_of_Tonga,"December 18, 2025 - Music of Tonga today generally falls under the category of traditional music that has withstood the test of time, or into one of the two opposing genres of religious and secular music. Tongan music can be either very emotional and somewhat modern with instrumental makeup including modern brass ...",Tongan,Austronesian
1,Tongan music notation - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tongan_music_notation,"October 27, 2025 - Tongan music from the pre-European times was not really music in the current sense but rather a non tonic recital (like the 'pater noster'), a style still known nowadays as the tau fakaniua. Therefore, when the missionaries started to teach singing, they had also to start with music from scratch.",Tongan,Austronesian
2,Exploring the Music Scene in Tonga: From Traditional to Modern,https://farandawayadventures.com/exploring-the-music-scene-in-tonga-from-traditional-to-modern/,"Older still are the sung poetry and chant that accompanied dance, including the lakalaka, a standing dance of speech, song and gesture performed by large groups that is recognised as a treasure of Tongan culture. These traditions are performed at festivals and important occasions, where the combination of massed voices, movement and rhythm carries history as much as melody. To an outside ear the older forms can sound austere at first, but once you understand that the words are doing the work, recording genealogy, place and event, the music opens up and the apparent simplicity reveals real depth. Published May 2, 2024",Tongan,Austronesian
